EN: This repository is dual-licensed. SOURCE CODE and JSON SCHEMAS are released
under the MIT License (full text in Part A). DOCUMENTATION and the SPECIFICATION
(prose specs, skill documents, catalogs, and other written material) are released
under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License
(CC BY-SA 4.0; summary in Part B). A private user's own Personal Agent INSTANCE
DATA — their evidence, candidate assertions, and confirmed records — is owned by
that user and is NOT covered by either license (Part C).

한국어: 이 저장소는 이중 라이선스입니다. 소스 코드와 JSON 스키마는 MIT 라이선스(Part A
전문)로, 문서와 사양(산문 사양, 스킬 문서, 카탈로그 등 글로 된 모든 자료)은 CC BY-SA 4.0
(Part B 요약)로 배포됩니다. 개인 사용자의 개인 에이전트 인스턴스 데이터(증거,
CandidateAssertion, 확인된 레코드)는 그 사용자의 것이며 어느 라이선스의 적용도 받지
않습니다(Part C).


What each part covers (적용 범위)
---------------------------------

  MIT (Part A) applies to:
    - Source code: everything under  tools/  and any executable scripts.
    - JSON Schemas: everything under  schemas/  (e.g. record.base.schema.json
      and the 14 user.* pack schemas).
    - Machine-readable configuration and example record files distributed as
      reference fixtures.

  CC BY-SA 4.0 (Part B) applies to:
    - Documentation and the specification: everything under  spec/  and
      skills/ , the README, CONTRIBUTING, GOVERNANCE, CHANGELOG, QUICKSTART,
      and all other prose/Markdown written material in this repository.

  Not covered (Part C):
    - A user's private Personal Agent instance data (see Part C below).

When a single file mixes code/schema and prose, the operative material governs:
JSON Schema files are MIT; Markdown prose is CC BY-SA 4.0. If in genuine doubt
about a specific file, treat it under the more permissive MIT terms for code and
schema and under CC BY-SA 4.0 for prose, and ask in an issue.


