=====================================================================
Part C — Private Personal Agent Instance Data  (NOT LICENSED HERE)
=====================================================================

A "Personal Agent instance" is the private data a user produces by running this
method on their own sessions: their captured EvidenceItem material, their
CandidateAssertion extractions, and the confirmed, scoped records that fill
their 14 user.* ontology packs and compile into their AssistantProfile.

Such instance data — for example, the records under a per-subject namespace
like  personal.<subject>.*  — is OWNED BY THE USER who created it. It is the
user's own content, NOT a contribution to this project, and is NOT covered by
the MIT License or by CC BY-SA 4.0. Publishing this repository grants no right
in, and makes no claim to, any individual's private persona, tacit knowledge,
or instance records. By default a user's instance data is private and stays
with the user; sharing it is the user's decision alone.

The reference example under  examples/logotekton/  is an exception: it is a
deliberately published demonstration instance and is provided under the same
terms as the rest of the repository (schemas/code: MIT; prose: CC BY-SA 4.0).

This carve-out concerns ownership and licensing only. It is not legal advice
and creates no warranty. See spec/04-privacy-boundary-model conventions and the
boundary/authority model (user.boundary_authority) for how instance data is
handled at runtime.
